# Project: wg-relay-manager

## Purpose

WireGuard Relay Manager is a lightweight management tool that allows a WireGuard Easy server to operate as a relay node and forward all client traffic to a remote WireGuard exit node.

The project provides:

* Web UI
* WireGuard exit tunnel management
* Route enable/disable
* Upload and replace exit configuration
* Status monitoring
* Complete uninstall
* Systemd persistence
* Reboot-safe routing

---

## Architecture

Clients
↓
WireGuard Easy (Relay)
↓
wg-exit tunnel
↓
WireGuard Exit Node
↓
Internet

Relay keeps user management inside WireGuard Easy.

Exit tunnel is completely separate from user tunnels.

---

## Components

### Web UI

Port: 8090

Functions:

* Login page
* Upload wg-exit.conf
* Start tunnel
* Stop tunnel
* Enable route
* Disable route
* View status
* Restart tunnel
* Uninstall relay manager

### Backend

Location:

/opt/wg-relay-manager

Files:

config.json
wg-exit.conf
app.py

### Command

/usr/local/bin/wg-relay

Commands:

wg-relay status
wg-relay tunnel-up
wg-relay tunnel-down
wg-relay route-on
wg-relay route-off
wg-relay restart
wg-relay uninstall

---

## Routing Logic

Enable Route:

ip rule add from CLIENT_SUBNET table 200

ip route add default dev wg-exit table 200

iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING 
-s CLIENT_SUBNET 
-o wg-exit 
-j MASQUERADE

Disable Route:

ip rule del from CLIENT_SUBNET table 200

ip route flush table 200

iptables -t nat -D POSTROUTING 
-s CLIENT_SUBNET 
-o wg-exit 
-j MASQUERADE

---

## Config Import

User uploads:

wg-exit.conf

System stores:

/etc/wireguard/wg-exit.conf

Tunnel restart is optional.

---

## Status

Display:

Tunnel Status

UP / DOWN

Endpoint

Latest Handshake

Transfer RX

Transfer TX

Route Status

Enabled / Disabled

---

## Persistence

Systemd service:

wg-relay.service

Restores:

* Tunnel
* Routes
* NAT rules

after reboot.

---

## Uninstall

Removes:

* systemd services
* web UI
* route rules
* NAT rules
* wg-exit tunnel
* config files
* binary

No changes are made to WireGuard Easy clients.

---

## Security

Password protected Web UI.

HTTPS can be added behind Nginx.

Default bind:

0.0.0.0:8090
